From 21ce83066ecb320e251c0473f76fac10b32a033b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: primez <mpincoski@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 01:49:23 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 7/9] [TSReader] Take the PTS offset from the first PES of a
 segment

The TS demuxer emits a PES only when the next PES of the stream starts,
and the video parser also waits for the start of the next frame. When
the session sets the PTS offset of a new segment, the reader still
emits the last frames of the previous segment, and the next emitted
sample took the offset. The PTS diff was then one PES wrong for audio
and two frames wrong for video (67 ms at 30 fps) until the next seek.
The session uses that diff for the elapsed time and to select the
segment of a seek.

The demuxer now counts the PES headers with a PTS. TSReader records the
PTS of the first PES header of the segment, of the video if the video
is enabled, because the audio of a muxed segment can start first. The
sample reader takes the diff from that PTS.

The demuxer tests share the AdaptiveStream copy and build as one
executable. Generated TS segments test audio with 1 or 3 frames per
PES, with and without a PES length, with the next segment present or
after a wait, and muxed video and audio.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
